!#/usr/bin/env bash

This is the Part 1 of the WeldonGH's Arch Linux autoinstall, btw.

Programs that will be pacstrap'd:
base linux linux-firmware base-devel sof-firmware git vim fastfetch networkmanager efibootmgr

User's name will be of your choice, as well as the password.
Make sure to uncomment the %wheel line in visudo.

Time zone will be Europe/Moscow.

cfdisk /dev/sda
mkfs.fat -F32 -n BOOT /dev/sda1
mkfs.ext4 -L root /dev/sda3
mkswap -L swap /dev/sda2
mount /dev/sda3 /mnt
mount -m /dev/sda1 /mnt/boot
swapon /dev/sda2
pacstrap /mnt base linux linux-firmware base-devel sof-firmware git vim fastfetch networkmanager efibootmgr
genfstab -U /mnt >> /mnt/etc/fstab
arch-chroot -S /mnt

